course: dictionary
lesson: 12305
title: One word, many worlds
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the subject they belong to. The same word can mean one thing in space, another in the body, and another in speech. Context tells you which meaning you need. «The coronal mass ejection sent hot gas racing away from the Sun.» The words Sun and space are the clues.
explain: Look at the words around coronal and ask: what is the topic? «The doctor looked at the coronal scan of my head.» Scan and head point to the body, so coronal means a flat view that cuts the body from front to back, not a crown.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Coronal is an adjective in these sentences, so it describes a noun such as mass, plane or sound.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: In space science, «coronal» means of the corona, the outer layer of the Sun's atmosphere.
fact: In anatomy, «coronal» describes a flat slice that divides the body into front and back halves.
fact: In speech, «coronal» describes a sound made with the front part of the tongue, such as t, d, n and s.
fact: A «coronal mass ejection» is a huge burst of hot gas and magnetism thrown out from the Sun, and it can make the northern and southern lights brighter.
exercise: «The coronal mass ejection sent hot gas out from the Sun.» In this sentence, coronal is about which topic? | Speech sounds | *Space and the Sun | The human body | Plants and trees
exercise: «The doctor studied a coronal scan of the head.» What is coronal about here? | *The body, a flat slice from front to back | A crown worn on the head | A sound made with the tongue | The Sun's outer layer
exercise: «The t and d sounds are coronal sounds.» What does coronal mean here? | Hot and bright | Made with the lips only | Round like a crown | *Made with the front part of the tongue
test: «The coronal plane cuts the body into a front half and a back half.» What does coronal plane mean? | A crown worn for a party | *An imaginary flat slice that divides the body into front and back halves | A bright flash of light from the Sun
test: «Auroras can look brighter after a coronal mass ejection.» What is a coronal mass ejection? | A soft wind from the sea | *A huge burst of hot gas and magnetism thrown out from the Sun | A joint across the top of the skull | A sound made with the tongue
exam: «A coronal suture is a joint across the top of the skull.» What is a coronal suture? | A burst of gas from the Sun | *A joint across the top of the skull | A crown worn on the head | A sound made with the front of the tongue
